    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0037" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v02/pg5"/>

                <head>3. Memorandum From the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff (Wheeler) to Secretary of Defense
                        McNamara<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d3-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">CM-359–65</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1965-01-04">January 4,
                        1965</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Evacuation of U.S. Dependents from South Vietnam</item>
                </list>
                <p>The Joint Chiefs of Staff reviewed this date their previous views regarding the
                    withdrawal of U.S. dependent personnel from South Vietnam in the light of the
                    existing military and political situation. They recommend that all U.S.
                    dependents be withdrawn from South Vietnam as <pb facs="0038" n="6" xml:id="pg6"
                    /> soon as it is possible to do so in an orderly fashion. This recommendation
                    applies not only to the dependents of military personnel but to all dependents
                    of U.S. Government or U.S. Government-affiliated personnel stationed in South
                        Vietnam.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d3-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Earle G.
                                Wheeler</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d3-f3"
                    /></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d3-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d3-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Country File, Vietnam, Vol. XXV,
                    Memos. Secret. Copies were sent to Vance,
                        McNaughton, the other service
                    Chiefs, and the Director of the Joint Staff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d3-f2" n="2" xml:id="d3-f2-content">
                <p>The military aspects of the withdrawal of U.S. dependents from Vietnam were
                    discussed further in memorandum DJSM-65–65 from
                        Lieutenant Colonel David A.
                        Burchinal, Director of the Joint Staff, to Assistant Secretary of
                    Defense McNaughton, January 18.
                    (Department of State, Vietnam Working Group Files: Lot 75 D 167, Withdrawal of
                    U.S. Dependents)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d3-f3" n="3" xml:id="d3-f3-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that indicates Wheeler signed the original.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
